# Keep React's type definitions out of pnpm's hidden hoist directory.
#
# apps/mobile pins @types/react ~18.3.0 (React Native 0.76); apps/admin uses
# 19.0.8 (React 19). With the default `hoist-pattern=*`, pnpm links ONE of them
# into node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules/ — it chose 18.3.28.
#
# next@15.3.0 ships styled-jsx type definitions that `import ... from 'react'`.
# Those files resolve upward, find nothing in next's own node_modules, and land
# on the hoisted 18.3.28. Admin's own code resolves to 19.0.8. TypeScript then
# holds two unrelated `ReactNode` types and rejects every component:
#
#   error TS2786: 'Table' cannot be used as a JSX component.
#   Type '…@types+react@19.0.8….ReactNode' is not assignable to 'React.ReactNode'
#
# That produced 613 errors and had `@irth/admin#typecheck` failing in CI since
# commit 5b92891. Excluding the package from hoisting leaves each workspace to
# resolve React's types from its own node_modules, which is the correct version
# in both cases.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
